==================== CLAUDE: START OF THE OBJECTIVES STAGE ====================
Setup: examples/train-t1-objectives.json = the platoon-matchup config plus 25% attack and 25% defend fights with a target
(armsolar 940 HP or armlab 2600 HP) behind the owner's platoons; opponents charge/hold/kite/orbit plus the objective-aware
strike and guard. Outcome rules (src/learn/objective.rs): destroying the enemy target wins an attack; losing your own loses a
defence; holding it to the time limit wins a defence; an attacker that runs out of time gets the usual timeout score.
Reference brain: the round-4 champion from the platoon run (v3, no objective inputs). Its baseline on 90 fresh matchups x 4 seeds:
  attack 67% win / 13% timeout / 19% loss  (vs guard 82%, hold 94%, orbit 63%, strike 67%, charge 51%, kite 47%)
  defend 79% win / 0% timeout / 21% loss   (vs strike 77%, charge 60%, kite 64%, orbit 74%; hold and guard never attack)
  plain  66% win
  by power: weaker attackers win 51% (destroying a target is easier than annihilation), weaker defenders 42%.
First experiment: train the unchanged v3 council on this mix to see how much the objective changes without any objective
inputs. If the gain stalls well below the plain-fight level, build tactical_v4 with target inputs (docs/OBJECTIVES_PLAN.md).
