==================== CLAUDE ANALYSIS, OBJECTIVE CYCLE 1 (rounds 0-1) ====================
What happened: 2 rounds of 14 generations (10.7 and 9.6 min) training the unchanged v3 council on the mix of plain,
attack and defend fights (6 opponents). Neither round promoted a child; no child beat the champion by the 0.01 bar. The
champion is therefore still the seed brain, and the identical-batch analysis (analysis_cycle1.txt) shows the same numbers
as the baseline. Reading: a council that cannot see the objective gets nothing from 8 children x 14 generations of training.
That points at missing information (or at unhelpfully small rounds), not at the optimiser; plain fights moved +2 in 2 rounds
once, so a null result in this short a run is only weak evidence.

Response (fixed doctrine, like the platoon commit doctrine that fixed the fleeing units earlier):
 - Attacker: heads for the enemy key unit with 0.4 of its movement, up to all of it with platoon commitment, and targets it
   once within 0.9 of weapon range (destroying it wins whatever else stands).
 - Defender: pulled back to its own key unit only past a leash of 5 weapon ranges (at least 600).
Identical batch (90 fresh matchups x 4 seeds x 6 opponents), same brain, doctrine off -> on:
   attack  67% -> 73% win, timeouts 13% -> 3%, losses 19% -> 24% (vs orbit 63 -> 91%, kite 47 -> 52%, charge 51 -> 53%, guard 82 -> 85%)
   defend  79% -> 79% (neutral)      plain fights 66% -> 66% (unchanged, so the doctrine is isolated to objective fights)
LESSON: my first defender leash (2 ranges, min 160) cost defenders 6 points overall and 32 points against kite (64 -> 32%):
pulling defenders back onto the target drags the fight onto it, where stray fire and splash hit the target. Defenders must fight
FORWARD of the target. (Also a build mistake: cargo test does not rebuild the release binary, so one measurement used a stale
exe and looked identical; always rebuild before copying.)

Next: train the v3 council on the objective mix with the doctrine in place (rounds 2-3). If attack loses (24%) fall further
or the defender stays at 79%, the next step is learnable objective inputs (tactical_v4) instead of fixed doctrine.
